{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-64998",
  "enisaUuid": "2c5a7084-2299-3f91-8fcc-db77a1bf5b4a",
  "description": "Multiple DrayTek VigorSwitch models contain a buffer overflow vulnerability in the acl_general_setup Add ACE function. The vulnerability is caused by copying the name field into a fixed-size buffer without length validation. A remote attacker can trigger this vulnerability via crafted input, causing a denial of service or potentially executing arbitrary commands. Exploitation requires valid administrative credentials for the device's web management interface.",
  "datePublished": "Aug 24, 2026, 5:08:03 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Aug 24, 2026, 5:08:03 PM",
